    {
      "id": 29092,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-27T13:18:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Really this is almost the same question as Brain Burn.  What he is asking is if having no ongoing cards in play count as no damage at all (and no damage can’t be increased because there is no damage to increase) or if the damage is combined as a single point of damage (which would be zero damage, increased to whatever amount).</p>\n<p>Basically, if you’d play three ongoing cards as giving a total of six points of damage when increased by one, then zero ongoing cards results in no damage; if you’d play three ongoing cards as giving a total of four points of damage when increased by one, then the zero ongoing cards would result in one damage.  The same effect would then consistently have to be used for non-hero cards that do the same, such as Pterodactyl Theif.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:03:03.272Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 5678,
      "topic_slug": "drawn-to-the-flame",
